!Sample_source_name_ch1 = SALE_parental
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: SALE
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: lung epithelial
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment (lentiviral transduction): parental control
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Direct-zol RNA Miniprep plus (Zymo Research)
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Illumina TruSeq kit for 50bp paired-end reads, poly-A selection, non-strand-specific
!Sample_data_processing = Illumina NovaSeq reads were aligned by STAR v2.5.3a in 2-pass mode to BAM files.
!Sample_data_processing = Picard tools v.1.114 used mark duplicate reads, add read group info, and reorder BAMs.
!Sample_data_processing = BAMs are indexed using samtools v.0.1.19
!Sample_data_processing = FeatureCounts from Subread v.1.5.3 was used to quantify gene transcripts and generate raw counts file
!Sample_data_processing = EdgeR v.3.30.3 was used to normalize read counts and obtain CPM and RPKM values.
!Sample_data_processing = CPM values were used to filter the gene list  down to the 12,887 genes with average log2CPM >0.1 across all samples. RPKM values were converted into TPM values.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19/GRCh37
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: counts_all.txt is a tab-separated values file with the quantified read counts from FeatureCounts. Each row is a gene transcript. The first six columns describe the gene, and each of the remaing columns correspond to a sample.
!Sample_data_processing = transcript_quants_log2TPM.csv is a comma-separated values file of the log2 of TPM values. Each row is a gene transcript and each column is a sample.
